{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1089971-rambling-about-the-deathlords-and-the-abyssals","id":1089971,"title":"Rambling about the Deathlords and the Abyssals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-08T14:42:14-07:00","id":1089971,"title":"Rambling about the Deathlords and the Abyssals","content":"I was just thinking about how Third Edition has changed the Deathlords and what this means for Abyssals once we start to get more concrete information about them. To start with, the Deathlords oaths to the Neverborn are now the subject of rumor rather than being objective fact. \u200bThis, of course, opens up the possibility of Deathlords who don't serve the Neverborn, with &quot;Deathlord&quot; being a state that a ghost can attain to, perhaps through a necromantic working. Also in an interesting twist, the Neverborn are no longer mentioned to be unified in their nihilistic urge to destroy Creation - no motive is attributed to them at all.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis puts the Deathlords in a new standing in Creation. They don't have to be seen as inherent threats to life and existence. The Mask of Winters is a threat not because he wants to destroy the world, but because he wants to conquer your country and rule with an iron fist. Assisting a Deathlord in his ambitions is not necessarily helping to advance a villain's plot to end everything you hold dear. The idea of a sympathetic or even heroic Deathlord is now a possibility. It could well be that the reason that the Mask of Winters hasn't advanced his agenda of conquest in Creation is because another Deathlord is waging a war upon his holdings in the Underworld, a war motivated by a desire to protect beloved descendants living across the Scavenger Lands.<br /> <br /> This brings some pretty interesting nuances to the Abyssals who choose to serve the Deathlords. Now, a deathknight's efforts on behalf on his liege are not inherently antithetical and inimical to life and existence. Instead the why and the how of the Abyssal's service and the ends thereof must be brought into the picture. A deathknight can be a just crusader as easily as a monster.<br /> <br /> Of course, for this to matter, the Abyssal needs to be able to choose his or her liege lord and negotiate the terms of their service. After all of the feedback on Second Edition Abyssals and the Monstrances of Celestial Portion, I doubt we'll see the Monstrances return as a way to control or influence deathknights or their Exaltations. Abyssals will need a greater level of autonomy than they can achieve with a gun pointed to their head. I think that Abyssals will still be Exalted at the cusp of death, but I think for reasons similar to why I expect Monstrances to be going away that the old &quot;choose between dying and being death&quot; bit will be dropped. Abyssals might still face a choice, such as between dying and rejecting their place among the living, but it will be couched in terms that are less of a moral condemnation of the deathknight.<br /> <br /> Of course, with the Monstrances probably gone and the link between Neverborn and Deathlord in question, this brings up the question of whose Chosen the Abyssals are and where they came from. Who does the choosing? I find it doubtful that the Deathlords do the choosing if the Monstrances are gone and something feels off about making the Neverborn the hand behind the selection process, but the Underworld has no equivalent to the Unconquered Sun. The way the Underworld was left underdeveloped in Second Edition doesn't leave many alternative options beyond the Deathlords or the Neverborn, though. One theory that I had was that the Abyssal Exaltations were grave good copies of the Solar Exaltations, spawned when the Solars were entombed and freed by sympathetic response to the return of the Solars to Creation. This theory puts an explanation to where they came from, but it doesn't put a will behind the one choosing.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Abyssals are the Chosen of Oblivion itself, picked out from their fellow men by a sort of resonance with the elemental force of entropy, stagnation, and dissolution, but this doesn't feel satisfying. All of the other Exalted can go find their patrons and ask &quot;Why me? What about me made you pick me out of the millions of souls in the world?&quot; Then again, the idea of shouting such existential questions into an empty void and hearing nothing back, not even an echo, is appropriate to some of the themes of the Abyssal Exalted.<br /> <br /> Whoever's Chosen they end up being, I do think the idea of &quot;redemption&quot; is going to be long gone. If your choice to become an Abyssal wasn't really a sin, then there's no redemption to seek.<br /> <br /> This is just something that I felt like putting down in writing. About the only thing I'm really certain about is that there's so much I'm looking forward to finding out about some of my favorite Exalts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:19:00-07:00","id":1089992,"title":"","content":"Well, the aspects of the Abyssals seem to be fairly straightforward in 3e. Now, there could be Deathlords who are not sworn to the Malfeans, but they would not have been the Deathlords who received the 100 Solar Essences as part of the deal with the Yozis. Instead, they may be the wildcards of the Underworld who would be wiling to lead rebellions against the Deathlords who have sworn an oath to Oblivion.<br /> <br /> The independent Deathlords would also probably not be disgruntled Solar ghosts but could have been anything from the ghost of a Second Age dockside prostitute who died of syphilis centuries after the Great Contagion to the ghost of a First Age Lunar warlord who died of old age centuries before the Usurpation. Their only unifying factor would have been a terrible will when they first awakened in the Underworld to change the Underworld. They could be allies or enemies of anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T16:03:29-07:00","id":1090015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1089971-rambling-about-the-deathlords-and-the-abyssals?p=1089992#post1089992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, there could be Deathlords who are not sworn to the Malfeans, but they would not have been the Deathlords who received the 100 Solar Essences as part of the deal with the Yozis.<br /> ...<br /> The independent Deathlords would also probably not be disgruntled Solar ghosts</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's no longer needs to be the case. Most of what you mention there is actually from First and Second Edition. Third Edition is free to break from that old narrative and go somewhere else. There isn't necessarly some deal between the Neverborn and the Yozis and the Deathlords haven't been mentioned as being the ghosts of Solars slain in the Usurpation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:23:19-07:00","id":1090047,"title":"","content":"Actually, based on the Core book I would suspect that the Abyssals are different from the Solars. Specifically that they were always a possibility to come forth and happened to be something new now, either because of the Jade Prison (or whatever) being broken or for some other reason. &quot;Conjured from the depths of a forgotten history, the Abyssal Exalted are the champions of death.&quot; The forgotten history part is the bit that makes me think that they were always a possibility. Possibly something tied to before the First Age, maybe even something from before Creation like Zen-Mu. We just don't know yet, other then that they are different and aren't directly tied to the Deathlords unless they want to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:41:00-07:00","id":1090083,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty stoked about some of the changes to the Deathlords. <br /> <br /> In my own games, I threw out the whole idea that they were Neverborn pawns who had to murder everything. This made them more interesting as antagonists, and also introduced the idea that you could enter into long-term alliances or negotiations with them, without knowing out-of-character that eventually the Deathlord is going to <i>have</i> to try and kill you. <br /> <br /> I am a rather less excited over the idea that Abyssal Charms are based off of the Deathlords. It just seems like their trees will be a something of a jumble of different themes and concepts, plus issues with introducing your own custom Deathlords, and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T19:07:11-07:00","id":1090090,"title":"","content":"I'm attached to the idea that being a powerful ghost dedicated to the ultimate death of the world is basically the definition of the title &quot;Deathlord&quot;, but also to the idea that the end of the world can be nuanced in a manner that lends itself to several variations that aren't all straightforwardly murderous.<br /> <br /> \u200bI've got this image in which the Bodhisattva Anointed by Dark Waters evangelises his state ideology to the surrounding powers, and has long term desires to preach it to the furthest extent possible, and while the intent of his system is to ultimately facilitate the world's end, it's more of an ideological, even metaphysical thing, than a case of tricking people into providing themselves as raw materials to construct his fleet of superweapons intended to sail around blowing everything up.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnything from the creation of a world in which people live just enough to leave sustainable impressions upon death, and since the dead require so much from the living to be fulfilled, life becomes a kind of commodity to be traded and exploited for the fleeting pleasures of the dead, to a kind of mysticism underlying his practices in which the accumulation of the willing dead in his corner of the world will act as a kind of anchor, weighing it down and ultimately dragging everything into the fathomless depths beneath the Underworld.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's still about the end of the world and/or all life, just with a bit more complexity than just rolling around killing everybody, and based on a message that a lot of people can be expected to enthusiastically buy into, partially because there can be something very compelling about the idea of being granted high status by forfeiting your life, and partially because modern marketing teaches us that large numbers of people can be remarkably susceptible to being sold on shit they don't need that is bad for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:13:04-07:00","id":1090887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1089971-rambling-about-the-deathlords-and-the-abyssals?p=1090083#post1090083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a rather less excited over the idea that Abyssal Charms are based off of the Deathlords. It just seems like their trees will be a something of a jumble of different themes and concepts, plus issues with introducing your own custom Deathlords, and such.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThought: Maybe we have the relationship backwards. Maybe the Deathlords just have particular manifestations of the powers to which the Abyssals may aspire. Like the Deathlords have only a limited slice of what the Abyssals will grow into, but they've just been at it for so much longer. Then any custom Deathlords are either tapping into a different subset of the potential Abyssal powers or expressing powers that just aren't reflected in the canonical Charms. Does that make sense?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:22:25-07:00","id":1090893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1089971-rambling-about-the-deathlords-and-the-abyssals?p=1090083#post1090083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a rather less excited over the idea that Abyssal Charms are based off of the Deathlords. It just seems like their trees will be a something of a jumble of different themes and concepts</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you remember what the preview PDF said about the subject?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">plus issues with introducing your own custom Deathlords, and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIssues such as not being obligated to take every Charm, or the fact that players of any group but Sidereals can come up with their own Charms, in and out of character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:17:19-07:00","id":1090912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1089971-rambling-about-the-deathlords-and-the-abyssals?p=1090893#post1090893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you remember what the preview PDF said about the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Different trees are based off of different Deathlords. So you have your First and Forsaken Lion themed defensive/soak/armor Charms, and your Lover themed Charms based around seduction and being a succubus.<br /> <br /> This seems like Abyssals will fit into a Sidereal-esque paradigm, with different trees being based on different Deathlords, which in turn means the Abyssal lacks a singular focus. As with Sidereals, even if you're a Chosen of Endings, when you decide to use Performance, you're using Charms inspired by the Maiden of Serenity. There aren't any Performance Charms based off of the Maiden of Endings. So this ends up meaning that way you approach problems can feel dramatically different, as your Charms may have very different themes. This tended to make my Sidereal characters often feel like they were playing against or struggling with their own themes.<br /> <br /> It's the primary reason I never cared much for playing Sidereal Exalted (or Dragon Blooded for that matter, where my Melee focused Water Dragon Blooded ends up with lots of Fire-themed Melee Charms). I'm waiting to see how DB's and Sidereal and others are in 3rd edition, but for now I'm a bit wary that Abyssals will end up feeling similarly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T23:48:54-07:00","id":1090999,"title":"","content":"It was more nuanced then that; it was about using the Deathlords as the standard image of what deathly hero powers could actually look like, to give them a solid cosmetic basis.<br /> <br /> It's not the same as Sidereal Castes or Dragon Blooded Aspects, because we know what Abyssal Castes are, and they're not distinguished in any way like those other Exalted. The difference between a Dusk Caste and a Midnight Caste is not as dramatic as that between a Chosen of Journeys and a Chosen of Endings, so I can't see the basis of their being much clash from one's gothic warrior poet having a bit of exploitative relationship stuff in there if they favour Presence.<br /> <br /> \u200bNever mind that the people who developed the model pointed out that it would be more than just one Deathlord per Ability, and that not every Charm needed to be more than something that functioned about the same as a Solar one.<br /> <br /> \u200bLook at the list of associations that were given for the Bishop of the Chalcedony Thurible, and consider if any of those might seem like things that one would get in Presence as well.<br /> <br /> \u200bI really doubt that it would be any more intrusive than the fact that numerous Solar cascades go off in about three or four different directions, even when they don't call attention to it like Performance and Craft does. It would be like getting a preview of the Solar Presence Charms that led up to the more seductive or sexual ones, and assuming that was what that Ability would be all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T01:18:08-07:00","id":1091012,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think it'll probably be more like individual charms will have paths branching off based on a Deathlord. So for example the abyssal version of solar plate is just what it always is about summoning armor. The evolution stuff like trapping someone in it, trapping someone in with spikes in it, as before only forcing the armor to fight for you are more on the grounds of you have seen really f*ed up stuff being around the Deathlords and being linked with the dead creates some rather interesting avenues for a power set that can be defined as, &quot;what everyone else can do cranked up to 11.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 05-11-2017, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}